  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#popover-focusing-steps\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dialog-focusing-steps\n\nThe former has - at step 7:\n> Let topDocument be the [active document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#active-document) of control's [node document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document)'s [browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-bc)'s [top-level browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#top-level-browsing-context).\n\nThe latter has - at step 7:\n> Let topDocument be control's [node navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#node-navigable)'s [top-level traversable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-top)'s [active document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nav-document).\n\nThe documentation for browsing context - https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-bc - explicitly points out how it's often wrong, and how we should use top-level traversable instead.\n\nI think dialog is right, here.\nAnd popover should be updated to match.",
